{"id":"b7fdda9e44b8297521ea5d13f38078d8","name":"test_ws_poll_info_receives_terminal_status_from_worker_thread[False]","start":1794843331972,"stop":1794843332075,"duration":103,"status":"passed","fullName":"tests.unit_tests.test_bg_job_register#test_ws_poll_info_receives_terminal_status_from_worker_thread","retryHash":"3b8b4af1a7ac9dec8847283961634708.a11374d4a00030b0eec33257b423cdd1","testCaseHash":"3b8b4af1a7ac9dec8847283961634708","parametersHash":"a11374d4a00030b0eec33257b423cdd1","environmentHash":null,"flaky":false,"muted":false,"known":false,"isRetry":false,"labels":[{"name":"tag","value":"asyncio"},{"name":"parentSuite","value":"tests.unit_tests"},{"name":"suite","value":"test_bg_job_register"},{"name":"host","value":"runnervm8axu0"},{"name":"thread","value":"3662-MainThread"},{"name":"framework","value":"pytest"},{"name":"language","value":"cpython3"},{"name":"package","value":"tests.unit_tests.test_bg_job_register"}],"groupedLabels":{"tag":["asyncio"],"parentSuite":["tests.unit_tests"],"suite":["test_bg_job_register"],"host":["runnervm8axu0"],"thread":["3662-MainThread"],"framework":["pytest"],"language":["cpython3"],"package":["tests.unit_tests.test_bg_job_register"]},"parameters":[{"name":"from_threadpool","value":"False","hidden":false,"excluded":false,"masked":false}],"links":[],"steps":[{"link":{"id":"18c298baa41434066b4413c945a5a1e8","originalFileName":"8a07dba1-2237-4a0b-aee6-4d18d89c8fbd-attachment.txt","ext":".txt","name":"log","contentType":"text/plain","used":true,"missed":false,"contentLength":201},"type":"attachment"}],"error":{},"testCase":{"id":"3b8b4af1a7ac9dec8847283961634708","externalId":"b26b2803a1572059e3c99b23587b1127","name":"test_ws_poll_info_receives_terminal_status_from_worker_thread[True]","fullName":"tests.unit_tests.test_bg_job_register#test_ws_poll_info_receives_terminal_status_from_worker_thread"},"descriptionHtml":"<p>A job finishing in its worker thread must wake the WS waiter in the main loop.</p>\n<pre><code>``run_command`` runs the job in a separate thread with its own event loop, but\nthe ``new_log_evt`` waiters live in the daemon loop. ``asyncio.Event.set()`` is\nnot thread-safe, so without hopping back onto the daemon loop the terminal DONE\nnotification is lost and ``ws_poll_info`` hangs forever (the desktop app's\n&quot;finalizing&quot; step never completes and the connection eventually drops).\n``from_threadpool`` mimics sync routes (``/update/start``), which call\n``run_command`` from FastAPI's threadpool, with no running loop.\n</code></pre>\n","environment":"default","setup":[{"id":"2827ab95e54ead7ba117fccf45625432","type":"before","name":"event_loop_policy","status":"passed","steps":[],"duration":0},{"id":"8e485d9eb95e72d531934c134a9b81ca","type":"before","name":"tmp_path_factory","status":"passed","steps":[],"duration":0},{"id":"3c52b9285de541b6611f81f1ca7da2c1","type":"before","name":"_no_telemetry","status":"passed","steps":[],"duration":0},{"id":"2f268d1247334a931895f857d23e80cc","type":"before","name":"_isolated_hf_credentials","status":"passed","steps":[],"duration":2},{"id":"58fea5b0f25e9bfd32681e6de65cf903","type":"before","name":"monkeypatch","status":"passed","steps":[],"duration":0},{"id":"6402838f8a6e38ae999bcb070b969b66","type":"before","name":"_function_scoped_runner","status":"passed","steps":[],"duration":0}],"teardown":[{"id":"4c12b57e81aea6265733b9d86257a0d1","type":"after","name":"_function_scoped_runner::0","status":"passed","steps":[],"duration":1},{"id":"7a466e6f5771727a7a1cc67e28a78d19","type":"after","name":"monkeypatch::0","status":"passed","steps":[],"duration":0}],"history":[],"retries":[],"breadcrumbs":[["tests.unit_tests","test_bg_job_register"]],"retry":false,"transition":"new","titlePath":["tests","unit_tests","test_bg_job_register.py"],"retriesCount":0,"retriesStatusChange":false,"attachments":[{"link":{"id":"18c298baa41434066b4413c945a5a1e8","originalFileName":"8a07dba1-2237-4a0b-aee6-4d18d89c8fbd-attachment.txt","ext":".txt","name":"log",